>> title: Frangipane
>> category: Custards & Puddings
>> tags: almond, filling, butter, make-ahead, no-cook
>> counters: Bakery
>> aka: frangipane, crème d'amande, creme d'amande, creme damande, almond cream, almond filling, almond paste filling
>> pairs-with: almond-croissant, sweet-tart-shell
>> servings: 12
>> time: 1 hr 15 min
>> slack: forgiving — it will not be beaten after the almond goes in: the eggs split out and it bakes greasy instead of rising

>> step: cream the butter, sugar and salt pale
Cream @softened unsalted butter{1/2%cup}(115 g), @granulated sugar{1/2%cup}(115 g) and @fine sea salt{1/4%tsp}(1.5 g) until pale and light.

>> step: beat the eggs in one at a time
Beat @eggs{2%large}(115 g, at room temperature) into @&(~1)creamed butter{} one at a time, letting each disappear before the next goes in. Cold eggs split the cream, and a split frangipane weeps butter in the oven.

>> step: fold the almond and flour through
Fold @almond flour{1 1/4%cup}(115 g) and @all-purpose flour{2%Tbs}(15 g) through @&(~1)egg mixture{} until just smooth.

>> step: stir in the rum, chill 1 hour
Stir @dark rum{1%Tbs}(15 mL) and @almond extract{1/4%tsp}(1 mL) through @&(~1)almond cream{}, then ~chill{1%hr} until it is firm enough to pipe.
